Akeno XII, my best samurai ever, finally met his end....

See, he was possibly my first ever character that looked ascendable without
an early wish, coaligned minetown, or even nice bones files.  Well, bones
helped a little, he picked up an Excalibur and +3 plate mail from them, but
nothing spectacular.  Because of the lack of an early wish, he had no SDSM,
so he headed lower, hoping to find the portal to ludios, knowing that
dragons usually hang out there.  Found the portal, and fought everything off
with his +0 frostbrand.  Killed 4 dragons, silver, black, green, and blue.
Found 3 scales.  Guess which one didn't leave scales?  Anyway, he decided to
find out if just scales by themselves were better than the plate mail, so he
went to put on the black scales.  Took off the CoMR, took of the plate mail,
and then was drowned by an eel while putting the dragon scales on.  I
suppose I should have unblinded myself, then I would have realized that I
had reached the corner of ludios, and was diagonally adjacent to water.
Sigh....


What really annoys me is that not only is this my first drowning, but it's
